#: ../../source/docs/common-reach-rtk-receiver.rst:14
#: a1c696a455534cd3829028f7bfe7c8d6
msgid "What is Reach and what is it for?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-reach-rtk-receiver.rst:16
#: d07373dda3694f878aee91d40cf5cbc2
msgid "Reach is an RTK GNSS receiver for applications when your standard GPS with several meters accuracy just won't cut it. It relies on RTK (real-time kinematics) technology to deliver centimeter level accuracy."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-reach-rtk-receiver.rst:18
#: 8044b92aa83544bd8b7192c3c9029f4f
msgid "RTK has historically been used primarily by surveyors and others who required centimeter precise positioning, and were able to spend thousands of dollars on an RTK system. Reach makes this same functionality affordable to hobbyists and makers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-reach-rtk-receiver.rst:20
#: c18aba79ed1b4e5da19ea8f0ced558c9
msgid "Reach runs open-source RTK processing software called RTKLIB written by Tomoji Takasu. Previously a computer was required to run RTKLIB, but now all RTKLIB features are available directly on Reach."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-reach-rtk-receiver.rst:22
#: c22149436795499b84f1010bea9b19d0
msgid "For further information see `Reach documentation <https://docs.emlid.com/reach/>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-reach-rtk-receiver.rst:25
#: d12d7896e07a41b28a0d4b4488c05cc9
msgid "ArduPilot integration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-reach-rtk-receiver.rst:27
#: 52f66c97c9a24c04870d15d2cf0fa8b2
msgid "Reach supports RTK-enhanced coordinates output to ArduPilot based autopilots. To make this possible, it uses a custom GPS protocol called ERB (Emlid Reach Binary protocol)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-reach-rtk-receiver.rst:29
